<body>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to main content</a>

  <main id="main-content" class="page" tabindex="-1">
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">Feline field notes</p>
      <h1>Cat FAQ</h1>
      <p class="intro">Quick answers to common questions about cat behavior, care, and everyday mysteries.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
      <h2 id="faq-heading" class="visually-hidden">Frequently asked questions about cats</h2>

      <div class="example">
        <h3>
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="true">
            <span>Why do cats purr?</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
        </h3>
        <div class="details">
          <p>Cats often purr when they feel relaxed, but they may also purr to self-soothe when stressed, tired, or healing. Context and body language help explain the reason.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <h3>
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="true">
            <span>How often should I feed my cat?</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
        </h3>
        <div class="details">
          <p>Most adult cats do well with measured meals two or more times a day. The right amount depends on age, weight, activity level, and your veterinarian's guidance.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <h3>
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="true">
            <span>Why does my cat knead blankets?</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
        </h3>
        <div class="details">
          <p>Kneading is a comforting behavior that begins in kittenhood. Adult cats may knead soft surfaces when they feel safe, sleepy, or ready to settle in.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <h3>
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="true">
            <span>Do indoor cats need enrichment?</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
        </h3>
        <div class="details">
          <p>Yes. Puzzle feeders, climbing spaces, window perches, scratching posts, and short play sessions help indoor cats exercise their bodies and minds.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <h3>
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="true">
            <span>Why do cats knock things off tables?</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
        </h3>
        <div class="details">
          <p>Cats explore with their paws, test movement, and learn what gets attention. Providing safe toys and clearing fragile items can reduce the temptation.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer>
      <p>For health concerns, ask a licensed veterinarian who knows your cat's history.</p>
    </footer>
  </main>

  <script>
    const disclosureButtons = document.querySelectorAll(".question");

    disclosureButtons.forEach((button) => {
      const panel = button.closest(".example").querySelector(".details");

      button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", "false");
      panel.hidden = true;

      button.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const isOpen = button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";
        button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isOpen));
        panel.hidden = isOpen;
      });

      button.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
        if (event.key === "Escape" && button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true") {
          button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", "false");
          panel.hidden = true;
          button.focus();
        }
      });
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
